    {"id": 6, "fact": "In City of Renton v. Playtime Theatres, Inc. (1986), the Supreme Court held that time, place, and manner regulations are permissible if they are content-neutral, narrowly tailored to serve a significant government interest, and leave open ample alternative channels for communication.", "source_date": "1986-06-25"}
